Package: NepInventory
Type: Package
Title: Tools for Forest Inventory Analysis in Nepal
Version: 0.1.2
Authors@R: person(
    given = "Santosh",
    family = "Ayer",
    role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "ayer.sant@gmail.com"
    )
Description: Provides tools for forest inventory analysis in Nepal, with an
    initial focus on post-inventory assessment of sampling intensity and
    statistical precision. The package summarizes plot-level forest attributes,
    calculates relative sampling error and confidence intervals, evaluates
    attribute-specific precision targets, compares observed sampling intensity
    with a user-specified benchmark, estimates plot requirements for alternative
    relative-error targets, and produces precision-versus-sample-size curves.
    Precision calculations are based on a simple random sampling variance
    estimator. For systematic inventories, this estimator is used as a practical
    approximation and should be interpreted accordingly. The package is designed
    to support additional forest inventory attributes, sampling designs, and
    Nepal-specific inventory workflows in future versions.
